{"abstract":[{"text":"Beam values include begin, continue, end, forward hook, and backward hook. Up to eight concurrent beams are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"available to cover up to 1024th notes. Each beam in a note is represented with a separate beam element,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"starting with the eighth note beam using a number attribute of 1.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/init(id:value:number:repeater:fan:color:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/fan","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/number","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/repeater","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/value"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbeam"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBeam","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that the beam number does not distinguish sets of beams that overlap, as it does for slur and other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. Beaming groups are distinguished by being in different voices and\/or the presence or absence of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grace and cue elements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beams that have a begin value can also have a fan attribute to indicate accelerandos and ritardandos using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fanned beams. The fan attribute may also be used with a continue value if the fanning direction changes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that note. The value is “none” if not specified."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The repeater attribute has been deprecated in MusicXML 3.0. Formerly used for tremolos, it needs to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified with a “yes” value for each beam using it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<beam>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeam"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLBeamV","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBeam","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBeam","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"MXLBeam"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBeam/color":{"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"title":"color","type":"topic","url":"\